  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA multi-profile with avgpool and PCA n2000 (config_002, acc=0.5907) is the clear best so far, outperforming single-profile (0.4849), transformer aggregation (0.5191), and image-only (0.2079). The only RNA encoder tested is PCA n2000. Uncertainty: whether a pre-trained single-cell foundation model (scgpt) can improve upon PCA in the proven best multi-profile + avgpool setup. This experiment (config_008) isolates the RNA encoder variable while holding profile=multiprofile and aggregation=avgpool constant, enabling a clean comparison against config_002. It is the best next step because (1) RNA is the dominant modality, so optimizing its encoder is higher-value than testing multimodal fusion with a very weak image signal (0.21), (2) scgpt represents a fundamentally different representation type (pre-trained on large-scale scRNA-seq) versus PCA, so the information gain is high, and (3) the result directly informs which RNA encoder to pair with multimodal fusion in the remaining 5 experiments."
}

